# Build context is the REPO ROOT (see backend/Dockerfile), so this file is
# what keeps the context small — and, more importantly, keeps local PII out of
# it. `inspro.db` is seeded with real employee data when placement slips are
# uploaded locally, and `reference/` holds real broker slips. Neither is COPY'd
# by the Dockerfile, but neither should be handed to the daemon either.
**/inspro.db
**/inspro.db-*
**/*.db*
**/*.sqlite*
reference/
**/var/
**/*.xls
**/*.xlsx

# Dependencies + build output — reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image. Copying
# the host's node_modules over the container's would clobber a correct
# platform-specific install with an incompatible one.
**/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
# `**/` matters: a bare `.mypy_cache/` is root-anchored and leaves
# backend/.mypy_cache (tens of MB) in the upload.
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# Not needed to build or run the image.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.21st/
.impeccable/
.pnpm-store/
output/
tmp/
tools/
handover/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/*.zip
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.pfx
docs/
infra/
*.md
!backend/README.md
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Developer-only tooling stays out of the production image: the persistent
# SQLite launcher, and scripts that seed demo identities or delete operational
# rows (each also refuses to run unless INSPRO_ENV=dev with a SQLite database).
# seed_demo.py must ship: app startup (app/core/drift_checks.py) and
# seed_firm_library.py import its catalogs, and its seed() carries the same
# guard. tests/test_release_guards.py pins both lists.
backend/scripts/local_dev.py
backend/scripts/dev.ps1
backend/scripts/reset_data.py
backend/scripts/seed_claims_demo.py
backend/scripts/seed_cdl_portal_accounts.py
backend/scripts/seed_portal_ui_review.py
